course: dictionary
lesson: 15540
title: Sunken
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Sunken has three meanings, and the clues in the sentence tell you which one to use. «Divers found a sunken ship lying on the bottom of the lake.» The ship is lying at the bottom after sinking, so sunken means sunk to the bottom.
explain: «The children sat in the sunken garden, which was lower than the lawn around it.» The clue is lower than the area around it. Sunken can describe a space that is dug lower than the ground next to it.
explain: «Her cheeks were sunken after weeks of being ill.» Ill, weeks, and the cheeks themselves are the clues. Sunken here means hollow and fallen in, as if the face has pulled inwards.
fact: Sunken means lying at the bottom of the sea, a lake or a river after sinking, as in a sunken ship or sunken treasure.
fact: Sunken also means lower than the area around it, as in a sunken garden or a sunken bath.
fact: Sunken eyes or cheeks look hollow and fallen in, often because a person is ill, hungry or very tired.
fact: Sunken is an old past participle of sink, so it comes from the verb sink.
fact: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «The pirates hid their gold in a sunken ship.» What does sunken mean here? | Hollow and fallen in | Lower than the ground around it | Floating high on the waves | *Lying at the bottom of the sea after sinking
exercise: «The children sat in the sunken garden to read.» What does sunken describe? | A ship lying under the waves | Hollow cheeks in a sick person | *A garden lower than the area around it | A cold, wet day
exercise: In «After a day with no food, his eyes looked sunken», which clue tells you sunken means hollow? | The ship lay at the bottom of the lake | The garden was lower than the lawn | *No food, so he was hungry and tired | The pirates sailed at night
test: «Divers swam down to find the sunken treasure beneath the waves.» What is sunken treasure? | Treasure kept in a sunken garden | *Treasure lying at the bottom of the sea after sinking | Treasure that is very shiny
test: «Her sunken cheeks showed how ill she had been.» What do sunken cheeks look like? | *Hollow and fallen in | Covered in weed | Lower than the area around them | Pink and round
exam: Which sentence uses sunken to mean lower than the area around it? | The sunken ship rested on the seabed | *The sunken bath was filled with warm water | His sunken cheeks made him look very tired | The divers found sunken treasure in the lake
